er-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115420" :question/id #uuid "a77e9cba-1e54-5206-88b6-f1eec27273c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115420" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953561/assets/410da7fdbf283aba57c2000a37c56a87e11ed1b1372183a1d3c808376dba495f.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-5,2).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-5)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 25 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{25}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{25}{8})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115420/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9a34b79-65ff-5f7b-a8ee-5f19424fd9b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115420"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11779/selection/0f0602be3d112b2beb3583cc679ece9cd0e5f3ae64bf94f55d97d746d982319e" :answer/id #uuid "a15b7557-05f8-5b69-a5cf-54ecee47958f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11779/selection/1462d2f3148a4399df3d7215a813a32004dcd56074125ca0f2f7fc4ac416ee75" :answer/id #uuid "b70733b3-64eb-556d-8232-f4cd9d857df1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11779/selection/13a70f0a5769f26c6226622199e543a5208806b43c0ba226086c914e4