he general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(4,-12),$ so we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=-12$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(-12) \\\\ 16 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{3})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{4}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11779/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9a34b79-65ff-5f7b-a8ee-5f19424fd9b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11791/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3" :answer/id #uuid "c265c5eb-cb51-56ec-8bfa-034d5154cc78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11791/selection/368b661f4d19f80bb512500c891cbc6ac5141db308d2af2f466ec2ac53f8886b" :answer/id #uuid "183df78e-cac0-5e5b-8eac-e6f5fd63e218" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-5y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11791/selection/00efa1cd86414df9a3ec3b6c62479031aeceb850f45b923621b5517e10309808" :answer/id #uuid "6576999a-6db5-56af-9124-f7a3ee3137c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11791/selection/b73c47d4951226b80a54488eab52e7320eb30b7936ac27682f3727aec331136f" :answer/id #uuid "d12dad0a-4764-5e7f-9332-8589e467cb25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11791/selection/bb63415823a3bf672bb5b3eeddd6f00d923d4395e2e267b21ff530b7b088a5b0" :answer/id #uuid "441d45dd-bbae-56a4-baa0-202afceddc99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=5y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11791/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa62b217-c207-5f64-ad02-c249a0aa2011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11791/selection/368b661f4d19f80bb512500c891cbc6ac5141db308d2af2f466ec2ac53f8886b" :answer-field/choices ["q-11791/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3" "q-11791/selection/368b661f4d19f80bb512500c891cbc6ac5141db308d2af2f466ec2ac53f8886b" "q-11791/selection/00efa1cd86414df9a3ec3b6c62479031aeceb850f45b923621b5517e10309808" "q-11791/selection/b73c47d4951226b80a54488eab52e7320eb30b7936ac27682f3727aec331136f" "q-11791/selection/bb63415823a3bf672bb5b3eeddd6f00d923d4395e2e267b21ff530b7b088a5b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11791" :question/id #uuid "cc8325c0-99fc-559f-990f-6f2194728a22" :question/math-academy-id "q-11791" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953561/assets/48ae8debc8c92587e19b6c1cb67e426ef2fcf8a91d75a694a117c5e649cbd3f8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is downward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-5,-5).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-5,-5),$ so we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=-5$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ (-5)^{2} & =4p(-5) \\\\ 25 & =-20p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{5}{4})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11791/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9a34b79-65ff-5f7b-a8ee-5f19424fd9b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11781/selection/09dfa139565e3603a9f31d8f65aeab0ea89c5d8596eabadba3f26c1fa8f2d13a" :answer/id #uuid "c687280c-e3db-5905-9405-a54945cca0cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11781/selection/9399dfb0c1d454b99d1b3a2965433f39937830d6b844c1d3b37db94cdb0521ad" :answer/id #uuid "3c940e4f-86fd-5d75-a839-d26d41c3d189" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11781/selection/13a70f0a5769f26c6226622199e543a5208806b43c0ba226086c914e42e59b7e" :answer/id #uuid "38781249-ac98-572d-8c2b-18ac9dda94fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11781/selection/8bd822ea04ed26a97919b7e964aab18e5462832f7fff7d987a8c761fd1bed421" :answer/id #uuid "cb6e93cb-9bbe-5ea3-826f-c17e6e71d7d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{2}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11781/selection/0f0602be3d112b2beb3583cc679ece9cd0e5f3ae64bf94f55d97d746d982319e" :answer/id #uuid "2a4909a1-6aa1-5440-9aa7-09f8b412e4a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11781/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9d7e046-79d9-5df0-9eca-2fca64ecb60f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11781/selection/09dfa139565e3603a9f31d8f65aeab0ea89c5d8596eabadba3f26c1fa8f2d13a" :answer-field/choices ["q-11781/selection/09dfa139565e3603a9f31d8f65aeab0ea89c5d8596eabadba3f26c1fa8f2d13a" "q-11781/selection/9399dfb0c1d454b99d1b3a2965433f39937830d6b844c1d3b37db94cdb0521ad" "q-11781/selection/13a70f0a5769f26c6226622199e543a5208806b43c0ba226086c914e42e59b7e" "q-11781/selection/8bd822ea04ed26a97919b7e964aab18e5462832f7fff7d987a8c761fd1bed421" "q-11781/selection/0f0602be3d112b2beb3583cc679ece9cd0e5f3ae64bf94f55d97d746d982319e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11781" :question/id #uuid "0d1ed87b-e125-541f-8d8b-9155dc0504bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-11781" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953561/assets/e588a9250583251ba2fd85b789eb3a856970fb6e7044289257a4ed97e3bbf1a0.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(4,6).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(4,6),$ so we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\ 16 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{2}{3})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{8}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11781/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9a34b79-65ff-5f7b-a8ee-5f19424fd9b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115415/selection/ae8320f65f5dba099d2a882be054b825ecf8277bd075c99859fc91ca980889a6" :answer/id #uuid "990397f4-d2c4-5fb2-8870-d1feed525c62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=9y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115415/selection/21a85a6c16cd09920557c85d675b32af6b265d2f20288e63723a698fa6039110" :answer/id #uuid "975bd0b4-681c-55a1-8f6c-6ce36fed2c39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-9y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115415/selection/e6f20e7a2c683e42ba58ae9b90ffa4a4f070767e05f928e749935ebf6d6fdc5e" :answer/id #uuid "34d473f3-8e21-57f2-8b27-24896af5998f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115415/selection/7e035f92a0a95e467bd3768435a97f7c01a73ed7be448724a02bd97073085bbf" :answer/id #uuid "b9151107-51c2-5e79-a235-18d1d54b4f28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115415/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3" :answer/id #uuid "520bddcc-7de9-5c34-8169-4b3872cba3a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115415/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba3a9320-0a9e-5b7a-8e31-95cffb38d468" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115415/selection/ae8320f65f5dba099d2a882be054b825ecf8277bd075c99859fc91ca980889a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-115415/selection/ae8320f65f5dba099d2a882be054b825ecf8277bd075c99859fc91ca980889a6" "q-115415/selection/21a85a6c16cd09920557c85d675b32af6b265d2f20288e63723a698fa6039110" "q-115415/selection/e6f20e7a2c683e42ba58ae9b90ffa4a4f070767e05f928e749935ebf6d6fdc5e" "q-115415/selection/7e035f92a0a95e467bd3768435a97f7c01a73ed7be448724a02bd97073085bbf" "q-115415/selection/9ccbc54c8a7c99aa32e755ee248a776c14d3fbbeb5548827e9593addab202de3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115415" :question/id #uuid "9d68b304-5abf-5a45-9d18-e5b77fc90d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-115415" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953561/assets/52b283fd5a8d9f374fad0a007f127598b86c53d7acf4df05d1415589e43faaa0.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(3,1).$\n\nFor any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,1),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=1$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {3}^{2} & =4p(1) \\\\ 9 & =4p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115415/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9a34b79-65ff-5f7b-a8ee-5f19424fd9b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115435/selection/b73c47d4951226b80a54488eab52e7320eb30b7936ac27682f3727aec331136f" :answer/id #uuid "6c782733-ebeb-5956-9c17-d28e8f15d7d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115435/selection/7a35be791bf0edec1186bc37a1baffbcfb47911c6487d7c1c870d96ec786ab49" :answer/id #uuid "5491da2a-e56b-5a17-86ec-3b184df4a7bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=4y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115435/selection/2d28f7475b6d9c613da2b98bb64da04459d879d07f6b7479be54a026e9fd1c43" :answer/id #uuid "c5838fbe-b90a-580e-b8a9-c21146e69279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115435/selection/dedaade2ccf88c4771f05068c6964825ef14b79e0a4e0091880c60253555f706" :answer/id #uuid "ee0d5dd8-367f-5471-93f2-9d7a1499a78a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-4y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115435/selection/eb2ad8e6962d492eb10f06b1b8a42f99535bac40a19b9361baae4f9c0ad69696" :answer/id #uuid "b72728c4-b12e-5c86-80